# 🚀 JavaScript OOP Practice — Session 2

This repository contains hands-on practice questions and solutions for mastering **Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) in JavaScript**.

## 📌 Topics Covered

### 🟢 Easy Level

* Understanding `this` in objects
* Default binding
* `call()` for explicit binding
* `apply()` with arguments

### 🟡 Moderate Level

* Fixing lost `this` using `bind()`
* Prototypal inheritance (`Object.create`, `__proto__`)
* Constructor functions & prototype methods

### 🔴 Hard Level

* ES6 Classes (Student grading system)
* Inheritance (Employee → Developer)
* Encapsulation using private fields (`#balance` in BankAccount)

### 🎯 Bonus Challenge

* 📚 Library Management System

  * Add books
  * Borrow / Return books
  * Track availability

## 💡 Key Learnings

* Deep understanding of how `this` works in JS
* Difference between function binding methods
* Real-world use of OOP concepts
* Writing scalable and reusable code

